course: dictionary
lesson: 10841
title: Verruca: a small foot wart
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A verruca is a small, hard wart, usually on the bottom of the foot. A virus causes it, and you can pick up the virus from wet floors. «Lucas walks barefoot across the wet floor every week and ends up with verrucas on three toes.»
explain: Verruca is a noun. Its plural can be verrucas or verrucae. In medicine, verruca can also mean any wart, not only one on the foot.
explain: Use the context to work out the meaning. «A verruca is a wart on the foot caused by a virus» tells you what it is. Then swap your meaning into the sentence to check that it makes sense.
fact: A verruca is a small, hard wart on the foot, caused by a virus.
fact: Wet floors, such as swimming pool changing rooms, can spread the virus, so wear flip-flops.
fact: «The black dots in a verruca are tiny blood vessels, not roots.»
fact: Most verrucas are harmless and go away on their own, though they can hurt when you walk.
fact: You can usually still swim with a verruca if you cover it with a waterproof plaster or a verruca sock.
exercise: «A verruca is a wart on the foot caused by a virus.» What causes a verruca? | Cold weather | *A virus | Wet socks | Eating too much sugar
exercise: Lucas walks barefoot across the wet floor. What could he wear to keep the verruca virus off his feet? | A woolly hat | Gloves | Sunglasses | *Flip-flops
exercise: «The black dots in a verruca are tiny blood vessels, not roots.» What are the black dots? | Roots that go deep into the foot | *Tiny blood vessels | Dirt from the pool | Seeds that will grow
test: What does the NHS say you can do to still swim with a verruca? | Swim with it bare | Soak it in hot water all day | Cut it out with scissors | *Cover it with a waterproof plaster or a verruca sock
test: «Washing towels at 60°C gets rid of more germs.» Why should shared towels be washed hot? | It makes the towels smell of flowers | *It gets rid of more germs | Hot water makes towels softer | It stops towels from getting wet
exam: Which is the best meaning of verruca? | A kind of flip-flop | *A small, hard wart on the foot, caused by a virus | A dark spot caused by sunburn | A type of swimming pool
